# Slipstream stage-90 patch series — applied AFTER Thorium's series and the
# Slipstream overlay, in this order. Format matches Thorium's series file.
# One patch per line; blank lines and # comments ignored.
#
# Windows exe output name. Thorium's chrome/BUILD.gn writes the Windows
# binary as "initialexe/thorium" and the reorder_imports action consumes
# "initialexe/thorium.exe". Those are PATH-glued, so rebrand.py's
# standalone-word rule correctly leaves them alone -- while the non-Windows
# branch ("thorium" as a bare word) does get renamed. Result without this
# patch: the exe builds as thorium.exe but reorder-imports.py looks for
# slipstream.exe and the build dies at the very last step. Must stay a patch,
# not a token rule.
patches/90-windows-exe-output-name.patch

